{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1421841347,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDcwODI1MDIw","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/33#issuecomment-70825020"},"message":"This is a symptom that we could see frequently, probably not every time coming with a nice workaround.\n\nIn my opinion this leads to a basic design decision: do we want people to work in annex'd directories?\n\nIf not, then we could use a \"crawler\"-like behavior for the generation and update of dataset handles. I.e. a sentinel job monitors a configured directory and reflects changes in the annex, but leaves the original directory untouched. Instead of a constant monitoring it could also be round-based and hand-triggered (\"now I am ready for revision 2\").\n\nIt get's more complicate on the consumption side of dataset handles. I obtain a handle `git annex get` its content, and get it served in an un-annexed directory, where its content is hard-linked into the actual annex. git annex could then monitor the \"detached checkout\" to identify modified/added/removed files. I have no idea how this would work in combination with meta-data based views of a dataset.\n\nNeeds more thinking...","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1421850719,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDcwODQ2NTcz","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/33#issuecomment-70846573"},"message":"also do not forget about \"direct mode\".  For datasets managed exclusively with datalad, and thus git-annex, we might escape all the symlinks madness by simply using direct mode \"installations\". Side effect -- without \"lean view\" ( #25 ) there would be empty (0 size) files present.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1421940748,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDcxMDM4MzI2","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/33#issuecomment-71038326"},"message":"Yeah, direct mode is there. And maybe that is what we should think about as a default mode of operation. Benjamin brought up that the git annex setup as a whole is more complicated on windows. Same goes for mapping possible workflows fro. Linux to windows. Maybe we should constrain our thinking to what is possible on windows right away? The thought alone pains me...","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1421951989,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDcxMDczNTU4","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/33#issuecomment-71073558"},"message":"Let me figure things out before considering such painful thoughts. The\nproblems I experience on Windows give me a fast track to a deeper insight.\nSo that's the upside for now. As far as I can see for now, the problem is:\nUsing direct mode leads to the question Michael brought up:\n\nIn my opinion this leads to a basic design decision: do we want people to\n\n\u003e work in annex'd directories?\n\nI have little experience with the targeted kind of users but I'm afraid\nforcing users to do or not to do it this way may be lead to low acceptance\nand lots of complains. Am I wrong here?\n\n2015-01-22 16:32 GMT+01:00 Michael Hanke notifications@github.com:\n\n\u003e Yeah, direct mode is there. And maybe that is what we should think about\n\u003e as a default mode of operation. Benjamin brought up that the git annex\n\u003e setup as a whole is more complicated on windows. Same goes for mapping\n\u003e possible workflows fro. Linux to windows. Maybe we should constrain our\n\u003e thinking to what is possible on windows right away? The thought alone pains\n\u003e me...\n\u003e \n\u003e —\n\u003e Reply to this email directly or view it on GitHub\n\u003e https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/33#issuecomment-71038326.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1455315670,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE4MzUwOTkzMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/33#issuecomment-183509930"},"message":"IMHO we should just have a documentation section outlining such gotchas and workarounds (env var for AFNI, direct mode resolution), thus marking as documentation and assigning to @hanke ;)","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1455315681,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDU0OTE0MTQxMg=="},"added":["documentation"],"removed":[]}]}